window.MENON_LATE={"changelog":[{"v":"4.9.0","date":"2026-11-15","stage":"release","items":{"en":["The Troy chapters: story chapters nine to nineteen. The main story now runs from Ios to the walls of Troy, each chapter with its own title card and rule","Play order matters: Setup (the next card gets stronger), Chain (stacks for each matching card in a row) and Finisher (a bonus for the last card of your turn). 27 cards rewritten","A new kind of card, Linger: it stays on the table, triggers left to right each turn and fades one layer at a time. You can also let it go","Aivenna is reborn as the Twins: Dawn and Night decks alternate each turn, with relays and shared immortality","New: Finish Off. When an enemy is low enough to spare, you can also kill it without playing a card. Killing and sparing now weigh the same","New: Struggle. With no card you can play, once per turn you can deal 3 or block 3 (not for Eurion, Vempolas or Odysseus)","Cleon: when you spare an enemy, every card in hand gains 1 Loyalty, so mercy no longer costs him his men","Kill boons reworked: Capacity +6; Max HP replaced by Expose on bosses at the start of the fight; Memory boons can go past the recovery cap for kills","Balance: Mnes and Cleon stronger, Aivenna and Vempolas slightly weaker; the Beast of Dreams regenerates 1 (was 2); Dream Depth 4 bosses +5% HP (was +15%)","Balance, round two: bosses can only be finished off at 80% of the spare threshold; Talos the Bronze, Guardian of the Lion Gate and Priestess of the Oracle slightly weaker; Agallos 56→62 HP, Eurion 58→66, Vempolas 70→76","Balance, round three: on Hard you now recover about a fifth of your used cards after battle (previously none); Act II elites slightly weaker: The Stone That Rolls Back Shield 4→3, The Faceless Phalanx Thorns 3→2, The Giant Who Grows Back Regen 5→4; Vempolas 76→80 HP","Balance, rounds four and five: Dream Depth 3 normal enemies +20% HP (was +10%); Dream Depth 10 -4 memory points after battle (was -6); on Dream Depth 8, Dread gives enemies at most +2 Strength per battle (previously no limit); on Hard you now recover about 30% of your used cards after battle (was about 20%), and enemies deal 10% more damage","New content: 53 cards, 5 enemies (including 2 Act II elites) and 34 events. Some events only appear once you have killed or spared enough","Fixed: the numbers on cards now include Setup, Chain, play-twice and Hold bonuses, matching the real damage","Fixed: dream cards Aivenna gets on the Night side no longer stay in the deck; the Linger card Unsent Letter recovers the right card; replaying an old chapter no longer replaces the next chapter's deck; auto end turn sometimes not ending","Much faster start-up (about 1.3s to 0.3s); the game follows your system's Reduce Motion setting; you are told if your save can't be written","New players: the first enemy is now a Trojan scout and the tutorial can finish; layout fixes for tablets and small phones; Korean changelog completed and terms made consistent across languages"]}},{"v":"4.8.1","date":"2026-11-08","stage":"release","items":{"en":["Fixed email sign-in: the code has 8 digits, but it was sent after the 6th, so sign-in always failed","Fixed the Wishing Well: entering it again while the result was still animating froze the result screen","Your current run is now saved when you close or leave the page"]}},{"v":"4.8.0","date":"2026-11-05","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["Story now has a Campaign: walk chapters one to eight with Seyagales. Each chapter is a fixed dream: read the first half, walk a short dream path (battles, story echoes, a shop or a spring), then read the rest and make the chapter's choice","Each chapter has its own rule (e.g. \"Three knots left\": recover 2 more cards after battle); chapter four ends with Mnes in the dream","Your deck carries from chapter to chapter; losing restarts that chapter at no cost; choose Easy / Normal / Hard","Finishing a chapter also unlocks it under Read; the first clear gives poppies or stardust"]}},{"v":"4.7.0","date":"2026-10-30","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["New mini-game, Kottabos (Events → Kottabos): the symposium wine-flicking game. Flick up from the cup to hit the little disc atop the bronze stand: dead center +3, a clip +1, and a hard enough hit sends it clanging onto the big disc for +2. Five cups a round, with wind; the first 3 rounds each day give poppies and stardust. Consecutive hits earn a streak bonus and the stand sways on the last cup; each cup is dedicated to someone, the reclining guests cheer or groan, and there are 3 new achievements plus a weekly board for linked accounts","New character, the Nightmare: no capacity limit, but every action costs life (a Burden each turn, playing cards, taking cards back after battle, walking the map). Only kills restore life, and it can never spare. The portrait is a placeholder silhouette for now","Defense cards have a new rule: once played they stay raised, and if the enemy's next action costs you no life (fully blocked, or it didn't attack) they return to your hand; only if it breaks through do they go to the grave. Each time a card comes back, its block drops by 25% for the rest of that battle","The interface now focuses on one thing at a time: in battle, turn, wind, held effects and the log fold into your row (tap to open); plays left are shown as dots","Choosing a character, god and difficulty puts one thing in the middle of the screen, with details under \"Abilities & talents\"; the title no longer repeats \"Enter the dream\"; shop, events and other stops only show life and silver at the top","Prefer the old layout? Settings → Game → Interface → Full info"]}},{"v":"4.6.0","date":"2026-10-27","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["Faster start: the first visit downloads about 510KB instead of 985KB, and a MENON splash shows right away instead of a black screen. Later launches take about 0.5s","Only your language is downloaded; switching languages fetches it and restarts (about a second). If you are offline and haven't used that language before, you'll be told","More app-like: no more accidental pull-to-refresh, long-press no longer selects text or opens the image menu, and the phone's back button or gesture opens the menu in battle instead of leaving the game","The screen stays on in battle and on the map (can be turned off in Settings); music pauses when you switch to another app","Saves: starting a run asks the browser to keep the game's data from being cleared automatically","Tablet portrait is wider with bigger cards; tablet landscape and desktop battles use two columns (enemy on the left, you and your hand on the right); on desktop, cards rise when you hover them","Holding a phone sideways shows a hint to turn it upright","The map redraws less often while you are idle, saving battery","Upgraded card names no longer appear in English in Japanese, Spanish and Korean; the returning-enemy event now uses your language"]}},{"v":"4.5.0","date":"2026-10-26","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["Your hand now scrolls sideways: cards no longer overlap, names are 12px and numbers 20px, swipe to see the rest; a lifted card scrolls into view. The old fan is still in Settings → Hand layout","Minimum text size across the game: text under 12px in battle drops from 45% to 9%, and nothing is under 10px; small text on deck, collection and grave cards is larger too","Easier to tap: menu, deck +/−, info and page buttons are at least 44px; undersized buttons on the deck screen went from 88 to 0","If you have no saved deck, after picking a difficulty you can \"Depart with suggested deck\" right away, or open the deck builder to adjust","Collection shows 24 cards per page with previous / next buttons","Achievements on the result screen appear once, with a glow, instead of also popping a toast at the top","Animation speed now has 1× / 1.5× / 2×; players who chose \"Fast\" are moved to 2×","Consecutive hits in the same turn play rising notes"]}},{"v":"4.4.0","date":"2026-10-25","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["The joker card, Mask of Momus, is reworked: Momus imitates the last card you played this battle and plays it again with doubled values, then mocks the enemy so its next action misses (its intent greys out and says \"Mocked\"). Still Light, so it doesn't use a play","New joker animation: the mask laughs in the middle of the screen, wobbles, throws confetti, then flies into the enemy's face"]}},{"v":"4.3.0","date":"2026-10-25","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["Dream Well animation rebuilt: the camera looks straight down into the painted well, a poppy falls past you into the water, ripples spread and starlight is drawn into a whirlpool as the colour climbs tier by tier","At 4★ a crescent moon appears in the water; at 5★ everything darkens, two heartbeats sound and the god of sleep opens his eye at the bottom of the well","Light bursts up from the well and your cards (with the painted poppy card back) rise from the water one by one and hang in the air; high-star cards have slowly turning rays behind them","The high-star close-up now uses the poppy card back too, edged in the tier's light, before it cracks and flips"]}},{"v":"4.2.2","date":"2026-10-25","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["Card recovery rebalanced: memory points now follow the value of the cards you used (before, they followed the count, so cheap cards almost always all came back); when you kill an enemy you can recover at most 85% of what you used, while sparing can still bring everything back","Each \"recover 1 more card\" bonus is now worth 4 points; the star map's Memory gives +4 per level, and Seyagales's Net +3 per level"]}},{"v":"4.2.1","date":"2026-10-25","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["When hit, the enemy art just brightens with a white rim instead of turning fully grey; follow-up hits in a combo no longer flash","A lifted card now sits above your panel, so your HP and block stay visible","Spring, forge, graveyard and similar screens are more compact, with buttons right after the text; the icon floats on a chessboard slab like the 3D map","In-run notices (achievements, tolls) now appear below the status bar instead of covering it","The collection search hint is shorter and no longer cut off"]}},{"v":"4.2.0","date":"2026-10-25","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["Attack animations now depend on the card: spears thrust straight, javelins arc, swords leave a gleaming arc, axes cleave bigger and slower, sling stones spin, rocks fall, arrows fly fast and straight, heavy blows bring a shockwave and cracks, plus claws, fireballs, waves, lightning, diving eagles, whips and flurries. Multi-hit attacks land in different spots","Kills: enemies shatter into pottery shards; elites crack first; bosses go into slow motion, gold light pours through the cracks, then they crumble","Sparing: light falls from above, the enemy warms in colour and slowly rises away while poppy petals drift up","In battle, your HP bar shows a striped section for the damage you'll take this turn, with an \"Incoming X\" chip; it says when everything is blocked and turns red when it would be lethal. Lifting a defense card updates it","With many cards in hand they overlap more so you can see them all; if they still don't fit, the edges fade to show you can swipe","The combo counter now appears under the enemy art instead of covering the plays counter"]}},{"v":"4.1.0","date":"2026-10-23","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["The in-run map is now a 3D chessboard seen at an angle: the ground breaks into floating islands, and you tap the glowing squares to move your piece step by step. Reaching a place takes you straight in","Each protagonist has their own piece: Seyagales's net-covered pawn, Eurion's die-headed pawn, Mnes's scarred rook with a shield, Aivenna's veiled queen, Agallos's laurel-crowned king, Vempolas's bishop with an olive sprig, Cleon's stack of silver coins, Odysseus's wheeled wooden horse","Enemies are ebony pieces (elites are knights, the boss is a king before the gate); a duel opponent appears as their own piece in bronze","Shortcuts are dashed arcs with their price floating above; tap it and your piece leaps across","HP, silver, capacity, deck, skill, blessing and whispers now live in the corners: tap top-left for your character, top-right for deck and capacity","Act 2's map takes on the colours of the underworld","Settings → Display can turn off the 3D map to use the old route list"]}},{"v":"4.0.0","date":"2026-10-16","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["Languages: added Simplified Chinese and Korean; the existing Chinese is now called Traditional Chinese. On first launch the game picks your device language","Card capacity: the deck builder, rewards and swap screens show a segmented capacity bar, so you can see what's left after taking a card; the run status bar shows it too","Fixed the title wheel icons jumping to the lower right when pressed","Sound rebuilt: music now uses ancient Greek modes on lyre, aulos and frame drum (battles in 7/8, bosses in 5/8); fewer, softer and more consistent sound effects","Star map rebuilt: one large, slowly turning star chart; tap a star to read and light it in the star card below. Constellation lines draw themselves when lit","Dream Well animation upgraded: the camera pushes into the well, at 5★ the god of sleep opens his eye in the sky, a shockwave, and your cards fly out and hang in an arc","Story is now a map of the Aegean: from the fishing village on Ios, the royal city and the harbour, eastward; the road lights up as you read (only places from the manuscript)","New special event, \"A Duel in the Dream\": sometimes another protagonist blocks your road with their own deck, drawing cards to attack you each turn and using their own skill on turn three. Winning counts as an elite fight","Security hardening: imported or downloaded saves are cleaned of dangerous fields and size-limited; error logs and nicknames are filtered too"]}},{"v":"3.13.3","date":"2026-10-16","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["Removed the \"Enter the Dream\" transition; pressing it now goes straight in"]}},{"v":"3.13.1","date":"2026-10-16","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["Fixed: on cards with long text, the keywords at the end were cut off. Text now shrinks to fit and scrolls if it still doesn't","When you enlarge a card, its full text and an explanation of each of its keywords appear below it","When choosing a new card, each card shows its keywords underneath"]}},{"v":"3.13.0","date":"2026-10-16","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["Interface overhaul: a new ancient Greek bronze-and-pottery look — buttons are bronze plaques, main buttons are terracotta, panels look like black-figure pottery with a meander border","Battle: the enemy's portrait fills the whole upper screen; your HP, Block and plays float above your hand instead of sitting in boxes; your hand rests on a dark wooden table","Map: an unrolled clay platter; places you can go glow, and you can tap the map directly","The shop is now a market stall: healing, cards, removal, upgrades and offerings in two columns, each with an icon and a price","Events and locations: a large emblem at the center of the shard, and Roman-numeral studs on each choice","Settings, character select, deck building, collection and results all use the new look"]}},{"v":"3.12.0","date":"2026-10-16","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["Character talents: one tier unlocks at Mastery 3, 6 and 9; pick one of two per tier (on the character screen, changeable anytime). Six talents per character, built around how each one plays","Blessings grow: after beating an elite or descending into Act II, your god offers more (choose 1 of 3, up to 3 times per run). Each of the 11 gods has 3 growth paths","Resonance between gods and characters: 8 pairings that get along especially well (e.g. Odysseus and Athena, Mnes and Ares) add a line at the start and an exclusive growth option","Balance: Mnes's attacks +4 (was +3), 86 HP; Aivenna 80 HP; Agallos 56 HP, Royal Decree 14 Block; Eurion 58 HP","Blessing balance: Zeus's first attack +2 (was +3); Athena 12 starting Block; Dionysus +15 max HP; Prometheus 10% steal; Poseidon −15% capacity (Eurion rolls 1 lower instead)","Enemy HP +3% to offset the new growth"]}},{"v":"3.11.0","date":"2026-10-16","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["Card overhaul: 38 new cards, 285 in total","Seven archetypes each get payoff cards: Combo, Shield as Spear, Creations, Wear Down, Held, Fate, and Sacrifice. Their numbers grow with the battle, e.g. \"+3 per card played before it this turn\", \"plus your current Block\", \"+4 per creation\"","Character cards: 3 each for Seyagales, Mnes, Aivenna, Agallos, Eurion, and Cleon, built around how each one plays (extra seconds, extra dice, silver, stances…); Odysseus gets 3 more support cards. Character cards only appear for that character, and the deck builder lists only your own","18 cards that were too similar or too weak were reworked (names and flavor kept), e.g. Shield with an Eagle, The Half-Pushed Stone, Three Heads, A Sip of Lethe","The \"choose an archetype\" start option now includes Shield as Spear, Creations, and Wear Down","Fixed Odysseus's support cards showing internal codes in their descriptions"]}},{"v":"3.10.0","date":"2026-10-16","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["Faster start: fonts now load in the background instead of blocking the first screen","Images use a smaller format and download only once; updates no longer re-download them","On a slow connection the game opens the saved version after 4 seconds","Fewer animations run at once in the collection and deck screens, so scrolling is smoother","The top bar no longer crowds on small screens (under 360 px wide); small buttons have larger touch areas","\"Start from a seed code\" moved into run setup","Errors are logged automatically and no longer freeze the game; copy the log from Settings → About to report it","Your save is backed up automatically and restored if the main save is damaged"]}},{"v":"3.9.0","date":"2026-10-15","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["Map locations overhauled: every place now offers several paths, each with a price","Forge: careful work, a roaring fire (upgrade 2 random cards, burn for 6), or melt a card into an offering","The shrine is now four altars: Athena (remove a card), Ares (−10 max HP, +1 Strength for the run), Hestia's Hearth (heal 25%, remove a curse), and a god's whisper","The chest is now three sealed jars you can only hear: a card, silver, an offering, or Pandora's jar; you may risk opening a second","Challenges can raise the stakes; springs show a reflection that copies a card; ruins let you bury the dead; dice take HP bets; the trader buys cards and swaps offerings for good cards; the oracle reveals the boss's weakness","Four new locations: Procrustes' Bed, the Muse's Song, the Three Fates and the Sphinx's Riddle","Enemy HP +3% to balance offerings and the new locations"]}},{"v":"3.8.0","date":"2026-10-15","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["Tutorial: your first battle walks you through intents, HP and Block, playing a card, ending the turn and sparing; replay it from Settings","Offerings (single-use items): Ambrosia, Nectar, Water of the Styx, Olive Oil, Feather of Hermes, Moly, Greek Fire, Water of Lethe. Dropped after battles or bought in shops; carry up to 3 and use them any time in battle without spending a play","Daily Dream leaderboard: sign in to cloud save and your best daily score goes on the board, under a name you choose","Seed codes: each dream ends with a code; a friend who enters it gets the same map and the same boss","Share image: make a report card with your character's portrait at the end of a run, then share or save it","Undo: within a turn, take back the card or offering you just used (↶). Results don't re-roll; can be turned off in Settings","Collection: search by name or effect, filter by rarity, change the sort","Bestiary: in the Dream Records, tap an enemy you've met to see its art, moves, traits and what it said","Color-blind mode: attack, defense and skill cards get patterns and symbols, not just colors"]}},{"v":"3.7.0","date":"2026-10-15","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["New fonts: Chinese text now uses LXGW WenKai, a hand-written kai style that reads like a storybook; Japanese uses its sister font Klee One; the MENON title uses the more ornate Cinzel Decorative","Settings → Display has a new Font option: switch to Plain for the previous clean sans-serif"]}},{"v":"3.6.1","date":"2026-10-14","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["Card frames are now hand-painted: bronze (1★), silver (2★), gold meander (3★), garnets and sun (4★), mother-of-pearl with wings (5★); upgraded 1–3★ cards get a glowing gold frame","Card contents sit a little further in so they don't cover the frame ornaments; long descriptions no longer cover the name and numbers on the enlarged card"]}},{"v":"3.6.0","date":"2026-10-14","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["New effect, Life: bleed your own HP to make a creation that does one job at the end of each of your turns for the rest of the battle (bite, block, heal, Weak, Vulnerable, or a fire that grows). Up to 3 at once","7 new neutral cards: Bronze Hound, Clay Warden, Athena's Owl, Serpent of Asclepius, Spindle of Fate, Stolen Ember, Daedalus's Workshop","Card frames now change with rarity: bronze line (1★), silver double line (2★), gold with meander corners (3★), a gold glint circling the edge (4★), flowing iridescent light with sparkles (5★)","Upgraded cards glow and carry a ＋ gem on top"]}},{"v":"3.5.0","date":"2026-10-14","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["You can now close the game mid-dream: it autosaves at the start of every turn and every route choice, and the title screen offers \"Continue\". Signed-in players can continue on another device","Burst: damage dealt in one turn adds up in the corner of the battlefield and levels up at 15/30/50/80 (Nice! Fierce! Burst! Godlike!). Your best single turn is remembered","Scenes and atmosphere: the shore at the start, wind outside the city midway, burning Troy deep in, violet mist in the Underworld — light, drifting motes and ambient sound change with where you are","New setting: Ambient sound","Your first two dreams are calm: no winds and no dream law, so you can learn the cards first. They appear from the third dream on"]}},{"v":"3.4.0","date":"2026-10-13","stage":"beta","items":{"en":["Odysseus reworked: the 4×4 grid now sits large in the middle of the battlefield, and tapping a cell fires an arrow (3 per turn)","Odysseus has his own 11 support cards (Scout, Fire Arrow, Volley, Quiver, Shield…), all free and costing no arrows","Email sign-in now uses a 6-digit code, so it works from the home-screen app too","Achievements are face-down cards: you see only the name until you earn one, then it flips to show how and the title","Settings: section shortcuts, a description for every option, vibration, high-contrast text, confirm early end turn, expanded battle log, save backup and restore, About and credits","Each element of the Star Map now has a star chart: the three constellations drawn at their real star positions, lit stars glow, tap a star to jump to it","iPhone: the step bar before a run no longer sticks to the top, so Liquid Glass no longer blurs it"]}},{"v":"3.3.2","date":"2026-10-09","items":{"en":["Blessing choices no longer include blessings the character cannot use","Vempolas plays no cards and never kills: only Athena, Apollo, Dionysus and Prometheus appear","Agallos in Shield stance (no attack cards) will not be offered Zeus","Daily Dreams and the Mask of Momus follow the same rule"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"3.3.1","date":"2026-10-09","items":{"en":["Odysseus now has his full portrait","The weakness grid moves to the right of the enemy art so it covers less of the name and intent"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"3.3.0","date":"2026-10-09","items":{"en":["New character: Odysseus, King of Ithaca — as he was when he first met Seyagales in the Trojan War","Plays like Battleship: the enemy hides weak points; tap a cell to aim, then attack. Hits deal ×1.4, misses tell you how many weak points are nearby, and breaking them all stuns the enemy","Skill \"The Horse\": gain Block, and your next attack is sure to hit a weak point","Added Cleon's opening narration"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"3.2.0","date":"2026-10-09","items":{"en":["All cards now share one playing-card format: portrait, the same face, only different sizes — in hand, rewards, shop, collection, deck building, the Dream Well and recovery","Card face: stars top-left, capacity top-right, name, and the main value large in the middle; tap ⓘ to see the full card","Card rewards are now shown side by side"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"3.1.0","date":"2026-10-09","items":{"en":["Star Map redesign: instead of a large twelve-sign sky, it now has four tabs — Fire, Earth, Air and Water — each a simple list you can light with one tap","Stars you already lit are kept, with the same effects"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"3.0.1","date":"2026-10-09","items":{"en":["Act II elites and bosses now have full illustrations: the Furies, the Stone That Rolls Back, the Faceless Phalanx, Kerberos and the Judges of the Dead","New key art on the title screen","The Underworld has its own map background, and the \"go down\" scene has an illustration"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"3.0.0","date":"2026-10-08","items":{"en":["New Act II, \"The Deeper Dream\": after beating the Act I boss you can choose to go down into the Underworld. Recover half your life and take back half your grave; Act I rewards are kept even if you fall","The Underworld has its own map and enemies: 6 normal, 3 elites and 2 bosses (Kerberos and the Judges of the Dead), all recruitable","Shades: enemies you killed in Act I may be waiting on the road. Spare them and they go","The Judges weigh your run: the more you killed, the stronger they are; the more you spared, the weaker","10 Underworld events, new endings and fragments, 6 new achievements","Dream Depth 1–10 (difficulty ladder): unlocked per character by winning on Normal or Hard; each depth adds a condition and more stardust and poppies","Character mastery Lv1–10: every run counts; level-ups give stardust, poppies and bronze/silver/gold frames, with titles at Lv5 and Lv10"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.8.1","date":"2026-10-07","items":{"en":["Menon's Renown now intimidates: the enemy skips its next action and gets Weak (+1 per 3 kills this run, max 3)","Bosses can't be stunned; they get 1 extra Weak instead"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.8.0","date":"2026-10-07","items":{"en":["Seyagales can become Menon: after 4 kills in a run, people start calling you by another name after a battle, and you decide whether to answer to it","If you accept: the portrait becomes the adult Menon and the skill becomes Renown (once per battle, 8 damage, +2 per enemy slain this run, max 30); the price is that you can no longer spare enemies","Refuse and you won't be asked again this run; new achievement \"The Name They Say\""]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.7.2","date":"2026-10-07","items":{"en":["Hero select: switching heroes no longer redraws the whole page, so there's no flash or hitch; the carousel swipes more smoothly","Battle rhythm: you can lift the next card while animations are still playing; tap it again to queue it and it fires right after the current hit (queued cards glow)","Playing several cards in one turn shows \"2 chain, 3 chain…\" with a rising note for each card","After a card is played the rest of the hand slides over to fill the gap instead of jumping; cards fly a little faster, and faster still when chaining","The enemy portrait no longer reloads during battle, so playing cards doesn't make it flicker"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.7.1","date":"2026-10-07","items":{"en":["Hero select: cards on the carousel are spaced further apart, so neighbours no longer crowd the centre card"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.7.0","date":"2026-10-07","items":{"en":["Setup before a run is now in steps: ① Hero → ② Stance (if the hero has one) → ③ God → ④ Difficulty. A step bar on top lets you jump back; no step needs scrolling","Choosing a hero: under the portrait carousel, a card shows HP and capacity as bars and plays per turn as dots, with the skill and the sparing rule together","Stance and difficulty are large option cards with a check on the chosen one; the difficulty step shows your hero, stance and god at the top"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.6.1","date":"2026-10-07","items":{"en":["You can now leave a run: a \"≡\" menu in the top bar and at the top right of battle offers \"Keep dreaming\" or \"Abandon this run\" (tap twice to confirm). Abandoning counts as a loss — you still get stardust, poppies and the card pack — but leaves no \"One Before\". On Android, the back button opens this menu during a run"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.6.0","date":"2026-10-07","items":{"en":["Run screens reorganized for phones: the top bar is now a single strip with floor, HP, silver and deck; tap \"Deck\" for details","Events and places (spring, oracle, graveyard, shop…) now use a scene card with an emblem, place name and story text; choices always sit at the bottom within thumb reach","Route: a shorter map with the hint tucked away, so choices show without scrolling; \"View my cards\" moved into the deck button","After battle: silver, recovered cards and battle stats in one card","Battle: the log is a single faint line; wind is a short tag like \"Notus 3\" (tap for details); held effects take one line and expand on tap","Buttons come in three kinds: main (gold), choices (parchment, left-aligned) and secondary (dark, e.g. Leave, Skip)"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.5.0","date":"2026-10-07","items":{"en":["New: The One Before. When a dream ends in defeat, the fallen dreamer stays behind. The next time a different character enters the dream, they come along and now and then step into battle: striking once for you, or putting their most-played card from that run into your hand (that battle only). Up to 3 times per run, once per battle; if you dream as the same character, they keep waiting for someone else"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.4.3","date":"2026-10-05","items":{"en":["Email sign-in is now \"send email → tap the link\": the screen tells you to tap \"Sign in\" in the email on this same device, with no code box for a code that never arrives; resending has a 60-second countdown"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.4.2","date":"2026-10-01","items":{"en":["More reliable sign-in: coming back after the app sat in the background no longer signs you out by surprise; if your sign-in really expires, you'll be asked to sign in again (progress on this device is safe)","Settings → Cloud save adds \"Sign out everywhere\" (for a lost phone); a normal sign-out now only signs out this device","Email sign-in: the code submits itself once all 6 digits are in, Enter works too, resending has a 60-second countdown, and wrong codes, too many tries and no connection each get their own message","Your account now shows whether you signed in with Google, Apple or Email","Security: the website only runs the game's own code; cloud saves get format checks and an hourly write limit; the developer test tools only open for the developer account"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.4.1","date":"2026-10-01","items":{"en":["When you lose by a hair (falling on the layer before the king, or with the enemy nearly dead), the results screen slowly shows one line: \"We are always one step too late.\""]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.4.0","date":"2026-10-01","items":{"en":["Story adds The Crossing, three new chapters: VI. The Knot, VII. The Eastern Line, VIII. The Horse (unlock after 13 / 16 / 19 dreams, or reaching the end 3 / 4 / 5 times)","Chapter cards now show their arc; each arc has its own ending, and a new achievement, The Crossing (title: Message Runner)","After reading the new chapters, three related places appear in the dream: loose water jars, a black and a white standard, a gray horse with a white face"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.3.5","date":"2026-10-01","items":{"en":["Deckbuilding now uses rows by type that scroll sideways: one row each for Attack, Defense and Skill, with upright cards side by side so stats and effects are easy to compare","The top row is your current deck (tap to remove); tap a card to add it, long-press or tap ⓘ for full details; each row keeps its scroll position"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.3.4","date":"2026-10-01","items":{"en":["All icons redrawn in the style of ancient Greek black-figure pottery: every map location, the title wheel, enemy intents, the small icons beside card numbers, card watermarks and the record book spines","New app / website icon: a black poppy, waves and a crescent moon on a terracotta roundel"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.3.3","date":"2026-10-01","items":{"en":["Dream Well pull redone: a stone well under the night sky, poppy ripples, water glowing stage by stage; every card you pull flies out of the light column as a streak of light (its color is its rarity)","More suspense for high rarity: at 4★+ the light is first drawn back into the well, a pause, a heartbeat, then it bursts; 5★ does it twice, with prismatic rays","New high-rarity spotlight: the card arrives face down, light seeps through cracks, then it flips and bursts","Smoother: the scene is drawn on a single canvas and the page underneath pauses during the show, so phones drop fewer frames"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.3.2","date":"2026-10-01","items":{"en":["Internal: added testing tools for development (normal play is unaffected)"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.3.1","date":"2026-10-01","items":{"en":["Playstyle tags when choosing a character and a blessing: characters show a difficulty rating and tags (e.g. Beginner-friendly, High risk, No deckbuilding); blessings show style tags. Also on the character profile page","Balance: Mnes HP 85 → 90, skill block 15 → 18; Prometheus steal chance 13% → 11%; Poseidon bonus +20% → +25%; Dionysus max HP +8 → +12","Text fix: Poseidon's description now uses the in-game term Expose"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.3.0","date":"2026-10-01","items":{"en":["30 new cards (reward cards 145 → 175)","New keyword, Tailwind: extra effect while the named wind is blowing; cards glow in your hand while their wind blows (10 cards, including the 4★ Bag of Aeolus)","More cards for rarer effects: Stun, Expose, Lifesteal, Trap, Delayed, Ruminate","New high-star cards: 4★ Wrath of Achilles, Whip of the Erinyes, Golden Fleece, Prophecy of Tiresias; 5★ Thunderbolt of Zeus, Thread of the Moirai, Hearth of Hestia"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.2.0","date":"2026-10-01","items":{"en":["New minigame, Knucklebones: under Events, throw four knucklebones against Hermes with poppies at stake (1, 3 or 5), up to 10 games a day","You throw first and may throw again once; Hermes throws after seeing yours. The Aphrodite (one each of 1, 3, 4, 6) is the best throw and pays triple","New achievements: The Aphrodite, Hermes's Rival"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.1.0","date":"2026-10-01","items":{"en":["Big animation update: effects that used to show only a line of text now have their own animations","Stun stars, Weak and Expose marks, the eye of Reveal, Enrage's red aura, Blind's fog, Counter's crossed light","Burned or sacrificed cards go up in sparks, Last Words fly out as a golden spirit, low-Loyalty cards crumble to ash","Momus's mask swap, a pillar of light for Hermes and the Styx fare, Curses flying into your hand, Cleanse's white sweep, Beyond-battle cards flying off as stars","Combo, First, After, extra or fewer plays, and cards returning to your hand all have cues","Outside battle: picking a boon, a new card, a shop item, or a card from your deck now gives a 'chosen' flourish; new cards fly into your deck","With Animation set to 'Less' there are fewer particles; with 'Off' everything is skipped"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.0.2","date":"2026-10-01","items":{"en":["Music now plays through Howler.js: on phones, battle music waits for your first tap instead of switching to the chiptune version","Music pauses when the game goes to the background and resumes when you return","Smaller page files, so the game opens faster"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.0.1","date":"2026-10-01","items":{"en":["New Roadmap: see what's planned for versions 2 to 6 under Settings → Update log"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"2.0.0","date":"2026-10-01","items":{"en":["New: the Four Winds. In battle the wind changes every 3 turns (north → east → south → west) and affects both sides. North: both gain 4 Block each turn. East: Weak and Vulnerable don't wear off. South: +25% damage for both. West: both heal each turn. The current and next wind are shown on screen; tap for details","Performance: images on the web version are now separate files, so the game opens faster and screens switch more smoothly; the Star Map background is drawn once; less live blurring and forced re-layout in battle","Email sign-in: you're told to wait a moment if too many emails were sent","Balance: with the Four Winds, enemies' +10% HP is reduced to +7%"]},"stage":"beta"},{"v":"1.16.0","date":"2026-10-01","items":{"en":["Battle music now has four tiers: normal battles are unchanged; elites get post-rock; bosses get strings and rock; the strongest bosses (The Name Menon, The Beast in the Dream) get cello and symphonic metal. Each tier has two tracks, picked at random each battle (music from Pixabay)"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.15.0","date":"2026-10-01","items":{"en":["Long pages like Achievements and Collection now keep the Back button pinned to the top left","The title wheel's center now shows a label for the selected option; the Star Map is redrawn as a real night sky (nebulae, the Milky Way, twinkling stars, shooting stars) and no longer jumps when opened","Dream Records is now a bookshelf of four books: Past Dreams (with filters), Character Notes, Bestiary, and Endings & Fragments, read by turning pages left and right","Story now reads left to right: swipe through chapter cards and turn pages like a book","Daily Dream has moved under the new Events","Character select loops endlessly, with cards arranged in a rotating display ring; main-god blessings are shown as three round emblems, left, center and right","The Dream Well's glow now follows the edge of the water, and the well no longer has a hard circular crop","Map nodes are now bronze coins with engraved icons, and reachable nodes glow"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.14.0","date":"2026-10-01","items":{"en":["New character Cleon (the noble of Ios): each card has Loyalty. Cards you use often come back on their own after battles; neglected cards disobey or even leave your deck. His skill, Pay the Troops, spends silver to give your hand +1 Loyalty","New main-god blessings: Poseidon (all card values +20%, capacity −20%) and Eleos (Empathy: while on, the enemy loses a third of any HP it makes you lose)","New enemy effect, Blind: you can't see your hand, and sparing has a 50% chance to fail: the enemy falls on its own sword (counts as a kill, you get nothing). Used by the Shade in the Sea Fog, the Voices on the Rocks and the Beast in the Dream","Mucha-style art for Cleon, Poseidon and Eleos"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.13.0","date":"2026-09-30","items":{"en":["After killing an enemy, choose one of three boons that lasts the whole run: max HP, attack damage (once per run), deck capacity, starting Block each battle, extra recovery after battles, or healing","Block no longer fully resets each turn: half of any unused Block carries over to your next turn","Easy is easier: 10% more HP and enemies deal 10% less damage","Balance: all enemies have 10% more HP; Seyagales capacity 76→71 and Young Eyes only returns cards of 4★ or lower; Aivenna HP 72→76; Eurion HP 68→62; Hermes' blessing returns 9 cards (was 8)"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.12.0","date":"2026-09-30","items":{"en":["New “Anonymous game data”: the results of each battle and run are sent anonymously to help balance the game. They aren't linked to your account; you can turn this off in Settings or delete what this device has sent","Security: Google/Apple sign-in now uses a safer flow, so nobody can trick you into signing in to their account with a link; saves are checked when loaded; the official site and app now have a content security policy","Privacy policy updated to explain what anonymous game data includes and how to turn it off or delete it"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.11.0","date":"2026-09-29","items":{"en":["Balance pass: heroes, blessings and whispers are now much closer in strength (simulated Normal win rates about 44–52%)","Seyagales capacity 80→76; Mnes gains “Veteran: attack cards deal +3”; Aivenna HP 64→72; Eurion HP 58→68; Vempolas must last 8 turns against bosses; Agallos's Sword stance now grants a third of damage as block and takes +10% damage, his skill gives 12 block","Blessings: Athena starts with 10 block and recovers 1 more card; Zeus's first attack +3; Apollo recovers 1 more card; Hermes returns 8 cards; Prometheus steals intents 13% of the time; Hades keeps at most 2 weaker followers","Whispers: Thanatos heals 10 and recovers 2 more cards on kills; Eris gives enemies +3; Hypnos no longer puts bosses to sleep","60 cards retuned: more block on defense cards, the strongest attacks toned down (Heavy Blow, Hero's Charge, Hector's Spear, Bronze Wrath…), sacrifice cards strengthened; Song of the Muse is now 3★","Enemies: Lion Gate hits and thorns reduced; Dream Beast counter 5→4; Sirens, Priestess and Chariot have more HP"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.10.0","date":"2026-09-29","items":{"en":["New card effect “Trap”: set it now, it takes effect at the start of your next turn. 4 new cards: Tripwire, Ambush, The Mended Net, Wall Raised Early","New card effect “Delayed”: it waits for a condition (taking damage, enemy at half HP, you at half HP, playing more cards, your next Attack) and takes effect once. 5 new cards: Tooth for Tooth, The Patient Spear, Gathering Breath, No Further Back, Rekindled","Battle shows your set traps and waiting cards; hand cards are marked ⌖ (Trap) and ⧗ (Delayed)","The results screen now shows the card of the hero you played; it dims if you lost","Suggested decks now come in four directions — Hero's pick, Attack, Defense, Neutral — and fill your capacity","Cards no longer change size when flipped","10-pull results show three cards per row, easier to read on phones","Store prep: delete your account in the app, privacy policy link in Settings, new app icon"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.9.0","date":"2026-09-29","items":{"en":["New pull opening: poppies fall into the well trailing pollen (three for a 10-pull), the water swirls, shifts color step by step to hint at rarity, and a beam of light rises; tap to fast-forward","10-pulls now fit on one screen in rows of five; cards arc out of the well and flip in real 3D, with rings and sparkles for 3★ and up","New high-star spotlight: the card glows and shakes in place, then spins to the center; its stars stamp in one by one, light sweeps across it, and it's marked New or shows the stardust it became","Reveal All flips the ordinary cards first and saves the best for last; afterwards you see counts per star, new cards and stardust — tap a small card for full details","Language is now a small button in the top-right corner (title and settings screens) with all four languages; the old language row in Settings is gone"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.8.0","date":"2026-09-29","items":{"en":["The title screen is now a bronze star-dial: nine options in a ring, with the twelve zodiac signs around the rim","Drag to turn and it snaps to the nearest slot; tap a slot to turn to it, tap again or tap the center medallion to enter","Below the dial: a note on the selected option (stardust, poppies, today's best, new story items) and an enter button","On desktop, use the mouse wheel or arrow keys, and Enter; the dial remembers your last choice"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.7.0","date":"2026-09-28","items":{"en":["New card effect “Ruminate”: after you play it, a weaker “Aftertaste” copy returns to your hand (about 60% of the values, at least 1)","An Aftertaste returns only once, can't ruminate again, and vanishes when the battle ends","8 new Ruminate cards: Old Wound, Ember Spear, A Veteran's Memory, Fleece Pad, Layered Shield, Lingering Wine, The Grazing Ox, A Tale Retold","Ruminate cards show ↺ in hand; Aftertastes have a dashed gold frame and fly back in"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.6.0","date":"2026-09-28","items":{"en":["Each run's text now fits the character you chose: road narration (early, middle, late), a line on entering shops, graveyards, springs, forges and shrines, after each battle (kill or spare), when the boss appears, and on waking — six versions, 96 lines","Lines meant for veterans (like “a song about a battle you fought”) no longer appear for Seyagales, Aivenna or Vempolas","Characters other than Seyagales always get their own epilogue"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.5.1","date":"2026-09-28","items":{"en":["The star map is now one zodiac chart: the twelve constellations drawn from real star charts in a ring around the Dream, with all 29 stars placed on real bright stars (Heart of the Lion = Regulus, Steady Hand = Antares, the Net-Mender = Alrescha, the knot of Pisces…)","Tap a constellation or its button below to zoom in; drag to look around while zoomed; Whole sky zooms back out","Three stars renamed to avoid clashing with real star names; everything you've lit is kept"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.5.0","date":"2026-09-28","items":{"en":["Redesigned star map: nine constellation tabs at the top (with progress and how many you can light), and the chosen constellation's sky below — no more dragging around; stars flare and the stardust count ticks when you light one","Three new constellations, nine new stars: The Many (a personal star each for Seyagales, Mnes, Aivenna and Agallos), The Well (more poppies, more stardust from Dream Well duplicates), The Sea (heal after events, heal after sparing, cheaper shortcuts)","Rebalanced: Memory Spring now gives +6 memory points (matching v1.3's recovery) and costs less; Steady Hand moved to The Heart and works for everyone; several stars cost less"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.4.0","date":"2026-09-28","items":{"en":["Remembers your last setup: Enter the Dream preselects your last character, stance and difficulty, and your last blessing if it's offered","New “Depart with your last deck” button, and the deck builder starts from your last deck","“Dream again” button on the ending screen","Deck builder: filter by attack / defense / skill / picked, sort by stars or capacity, tap a card to add one","Route: tap a glowing map node to go there; long maps scroll to where you are; the shop's Leave button stays at the bottom","Battle: optional one-tap play in Settings; long-press a hand card for its full text; unplayable cards say why; End Turn glows when nothing is left to play"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.3.1","date":"2026-09-27","items":{"en":["More silver: start with 20; normal battles 14 → 18, elites 28 → 36; sparing gives half (was a third)","Cheaper shop: heal 20 → 15, random card 25 → 20, remove 30 → 25, upgrade 40 → 30; graveyard buy-backs cost a little less","In simulation, the median silver when entering a shop went from 25 to 53 — about two or three purchases"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.3.0","date":"2026-09-27","items":{"en":["Recovering used cards now uses memory points: each card costs points by stars (1★ = 4, +1 per extra star). Take several cheap cards or a few strong ones","Every 2 unused memory points become 1 silver, so you can leave cards you don't want in the dream","Redesigned recovery screen: identical cards stack in one row with − / + steppers, a memory bar, Suggest and Clear buttons, a hand-size preview, and tap a card for its full text"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.2.0","date":"2026-09-26","items":{"en":["New Story mode: five Ios chapters (The Net, The Name, The Stables, The Scar, East) unlock as you keep dreaming, each ending in a small choice","Chapters you've read leave echoes in the dream: a net three knots short, a boy carrying spears, a tablet sealed with black wax…","Each of the six characters has two new events only they can meet","At the end of a dream, Athena and Oizys sometimes speak","Some characters say something when they meet certain enemies","A few hidden secrets and hidden achievements (hints: the title screen, a number, a name)","Fix: reward text on the achievements page"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.1.0","date":"2026-09-26","items":{"en":["Battle screen redesign: the enemy portrait is now the stage, intents show a big icon and number (red when lethal), block is a shield on the HP bar","Impact: hit-stop, white flash, knockback, damage-scaled screen shake, big damage numbers, HP bars leave a trailing chunk; heavy hits add a shockwave and phone vibration","Enemies wind up before lunging; defeated portraits shatter, spared ones rise in gold light","Drag cards upward to play them; attacks lock onto the enemy and cards fly in an arc","Encounter title cards, screen wipes between scenes, and a map marker that walks to the node you pick","Buttons press in and spring back; victory banner and silver flying into the status bar"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.0.2","date":"2026-09-26","items":{"en":["The 10 bosses and elites have full portraits: shown in the middle of battle, as their avatar, and large when you tap the avatar","Each of the 9 gods now has an emblem beside their blessing","The Dream Well has a painted well and card back; the route map has a faint sea-chart texture","The Mask of Momus card shows a mask icon"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.0.1","date":"2026-09-26","items":{"en":["Character select is now a swipeable card carousel; tap a card to flip it and read the profile","The Dream Well has a full-screen pull animation with a close-up for 4★ and 5★","Layout pass on every screen: clearer settings, compact achievement banners, the shop says why you can't buy, easier-to-read records","Version number on the title screen and an update log in Settings"]},"stage":"alpha"},{"v":"1.0.0","date":"2026-09-26","items":{"en":["Live at its own address; can be added to your phone's home screen","Cloud save: sign in with email and progress syncs automatically","Dream Well: pull cards with poppies, published rates and pity","Each dream has 9–12 layers with shortcuts and long roads, plus springs, battlefield ruins, bone dice, traders, oracles and mist","Character profile pages"]},"stage":"alpha"}],"story":{"glossary":{"cats":[{"id":"people","name":{"en":"People"}},{"id":"places","name":{"en":"Places"}},{"id":"things","name":{"en":"Things and customs"}},{"id":"words","name":{"en":"Names and words"}}],"entries":[{"id":"seyagales","cat":"people","ch":"net","name":{"en":"Seyagales"},"story":{"en":"A boy who grew up in a fishing village on the shore of Ios. He can count but cannot read. At twelve he was taken by men from the palace and put on a ship for Troy."}},{"id":"mnes","cat":"people","ch":"scar","name":{"en":"Mnes"},"story":{"en":"An old soldier with a scar from his left ear to the corner of his mouth. He says little, and what he says is useful. He kept Seyagales close from the first day."}},{"id":"lykos","cat":"people","ch":"stables","name":{"en":"Lykos"},"story":{"en":"The boy from the stables with a missing front tooth and too many questions. His favorite story was about the bulls his uncle saw on Crete."}},{"id":"pheres","cat":"people","ch":"stables","name":{"en":"Pheres"},"story":{"en":"A boy with a scar on his chin who keeps to himself. He says little, but he is always there."}},{"id":"agallos","cat":"people","ch":"tablet","name":{"en":"Agallos"},"story":{"en":"The king of Ios. On a board sealed with black wax he acknowledged Seyagales as his son. Why he sent him to Troy anyway, he never quite said."}},{"id":"peisandros","cat":"people","ch":"winter","name":{"en":"Peisandros"},"story":{"en":"Cleon's nephew, who commanded the men of Ios at Troy. He ate well. In the third year he attacked the Scaean gate without orders and did not come back."}},{"id":"alkmes","cat":"people","ch":"alkmes","name":{"en":"Alkmes"},"story":{"en":"A noble of Ios. When the grain was running out he had eleven jars of barley under his bed, and refused in front of everyone to share them with the shore men."}},{"id":"amphios","cat":"people","ch":"alkmes","name":{"en":"Amphios"},"story":{"en":"The boy with the bundle of spears who looked back on the day the palace men came to the village. Later, at Troy, he carried out the sentence on Alkmes."}},{"id":"eurion","cat":"people","ch":"eurion","name":{"en":"Eurion"},"story":{"en":"The man who brought forty reinforcements from the western hills of Ios. He had fought pirates and did not like it. He expected a monster or a puppet, and found a boy counting jars."}},{"id":"hector","cat":"people","ch":"truce","name":{"en":"Hector"},"story":{"en":"The Trojan who washed his own dead with his own hands across the river on the day of the truce. He told Seyagales, \"That is a name for a fisherman.\""},"hist":{"en":"In Homer's Iliad, the eldest son of King Priam and Troy's greatest warrior. He is killed by Achilles, and his body is dragged behind a chariot. The poem's last line is his funeral."}},{"id":"odysseus","cat":"people","ch":"water","name":{"en":"Odysseus"},"story":{"en":"He sat in front of the Ios hut as if it were his. He liked a man who watched the women go to the well rather than come back, and a commander who said \"I don't know.\""},"hist":{"en":"King of the island of Ithaca, Homer's hero of cunning. The Odyssey tells how, after the Trojan War, it took him ten more years to get home."}},{"id":"achilles","cat":"people","ch":"oldman","name":{"en":"Achilles"},"story":{"en":"The army's greatest warrior. After Hector's death, Seyagales stood sentry at the edge of his camp. When he died, the army's line broke."},"hist":{"en":"Son of the goddess Thetis and the mortal Peleus, leader of the Myrmidons. The first word of the Iliad is his \"wrath.\" Homer does not tell his death; the arrow in the heel comes from much later tellings."}},{"id":"priam","cat":"people","ch":"oldman","name":{"en":"Priam"},"story":{"en":"The old man who drove a mule cart into the camp at midnight. Seyagales should have stopped him, and let him pass. Later he knelt and kissed the hands of the man who had killed his son."},"hist":{"en":"King of Troy, father of Hector. In the last book of the Iliad, guided by a god, he crosses the enemy camp at night to ransom his son's body from Achilles, and kisses the hands that killed his son."}},{"id":"ios","cat":"places","ch":"net","name":{"en":"Ios"},"story":{"en":"Seyagales's home. The palace sits on the hilltop; the fishing village lies on the shore below. It owed Mycenae six hundred men."},"hist":{"en":"A real small island in the Cyclades of the Aegean. An ancient tradition says Homer is buried there."}},{"id":"troy","cat":"places","ch":"horse","name":{"en":"Troy"},"story":{"en":"The city across the strait. The hill on Ios had learned to command; these walls had learned something worse: to wait."},"hist":{"en":"The mound of Hisarlik in northwest Turkey. Dug since the 1870s, it holds many cities stacked on one another. The layers from about 1300–1180 BC are often linked with the legend of the Trojan War. Homer also calls it Ilion."}},{"id":"crete","cat":"places","ch":"count","name":{"en":"Crete"},"story":{"en":"Where Lykos's uncle saw the bulls. Lykos talked about it the whole way."},"hist":{"en":"The largest island in the southern Aegean. The Bronze Age palace at Knossos left a fresco of youths leaping over a bull, and the myth of the Minotaur comes from here."}},{"id":"mycenae","cat":"places","ch":"line","name":{"en":"Mycenae"},"story":{"en":"The great power that gathered the army against Troy. Ios owed it six hundred men, so even twelve-year-olds were taken."},"hist":{"en":"A Bronze Age citadel on the Greek mainland, its gate carved with two lions (about 1250 BC). In Homer it is the city of Agamemnon, leader of the army. The whole age is called Mycenaean after it."}},{"id":"scaean","cat":"places","ch":"tablet","name":{"en":"The Scaean gate"},"story":{"en":"A gate of Troy. Peisandros attacked it without orders, and forty-one men of Ios died."},"hist":{"en":"Troy's most important gate in the Iliad. Hector says goodbye to his wife here, and is killed by Achilles in front of it."}},{"id":"camp","cat":"places","ch":"winter","name":{"en":"The camp on the beach"},"story":{"en":"Over ten years the camp became a town, with its own roads, market and sickness. Ios got the flat, stinking ground; its stinking ditch became a wall."},"hist":{"en":"In the Iliad, the army drags its ships up onto the beach and builds a wall and ditch in front of them. The Trojans reaching the ships to burn them is the most desperate moment in the poem."}},{"id":"wax_board","cat":"things","ch":"stables","name":{"en":"The board sealed with black wax"},"story":{"en":"Seyagales carried a board sealed with black wax into the palace. Years later at Troy, Mnes brought out another. Both held words he could not read."},"hist":{"en":"The only mention of writing in Homer: the hero Bellerophon is sent to deliver a \"folded tablet\" that tells its reader to kill him. The one who carries the message does not know what it says."}},{"id":"clay_tablet","cat":"things","ch":"count","name":{"en":"Clay tablets"},"story":{"en":"The scribe read from the tablet: Ios, twelve ships, six hundred men. Seyagales had counted four hundred and eighty-seven."},"hist":{"en":"Mycenaean palaces recorded people, sheep, barley and bronze, item by item, on clay tablets in a script called Linear B. The tablets were not fired; they survived because the palaces burned. In 1952 Michael Ventris showed the script was an early form of Greek."}},{"id":"herald","cat":"things","ch":"count","name":{"en":"Heralds"},"story":{"en":"The men who walked the lines with a scribe, counting. Also the men who carried word between the armies during a truce."},"hist":{"en":"Homer's heralds carry a staff and are held to be under the gods' protection; even enemies must not harm them. They call assemblies, announce orders and arrange truces."}},{"id":"bronze","cat":"things","ch":"east","name":{"en":"Bronze"},"story":{"en":"Helmets, spearheads, swords: all bronze. A shard of bronze in the sand left a new-moon scar on Seyagales's heel."},"hist":{"en":"An alloy of copper and tin. Tin was rare and came by ship from far away, so bronze was costly, and whoever had bronze had power. The Trojan War story is set at the end of the Bronze Age."}},{"id":"truce_dead","cat":"things","ch":"truce","name":{"en":"The truce for the dead"},"story":{"en":"Both armies stopped to gather their dead. Mnes told Seyagales to wash their faces, \"so the men can see who they are.\""},"hist":{"en":"In Book 7 of the Iliad, the armies agree to a truce to gather and burn their dead. Washing the dead and burying them properly mattered deeply to the ancient Greeks; leaving a body unburied was the worst insult."}},{"id":"catalogue","cat":"things","ch":"count","name":{"en":"The count and the Catalogue of Ships"},"story":{"en":"The tablet said six hundred; Seyagales counted four hundred and eighty-seven. From then on he kept every man's name. By the end there were three hundred and seventy-nine."},"hist":{"en":"Book 2 of the Iliad has a long \"Catalogue of Ships,\" listing place by place who brought how many ships, about 1,186 in all. The poem records the ships and the leaders, not every man at the oar."}},{"id":"wooden_horse","cat":"things","ch":"wooden_horse","name":{"en":"The wooden horse"},"story":{"en":"The army burned its camp, pretended to leave, and came back in the dark. The city fell. Seyagales took nothing from Troy."},"hist":{"en":"The Iliad ends with Hector's funeral and never shows the horse. The horse is mentioned in the Odyssey, and told most fully much later by the Roman poet Virgil in the Aeneid."}},{"id":"fisherman","cat":"words","ch":"truce","name":{"en":"A name for a fisherman"},"story":{"en":"What Hector said on hearing \"Seyagales.\" Seyagales said, \"I am a fisherman.\" Hector said, \"Not here.\""}},{"id":"menis","cat":"words","ch":"menis","name":{"en":"mēnis (wrath)"},"story":{"en":"The Trojans' name for the men of Ios, which the army took up: the Wrath of Ios. Seyagales hated it."},"hist":{"en":"Ancient Greek μῆνις, the first word of the Iliad: \"Sing, goddess, the wrath of Achilles.\" It is used mostly of gods: an anger that does not stop and brings ruin."}},{"id":"nobody","cat":"words","ch":"menis","name":{"en":"\"Nobody\""},"story":{"en":"At a fire, Odysseus said he once told a man his name was Nobody. \"No one can hold it against you.\""},"hist":{"en":"Odyssey Book 9: trapped in the cave of the Cyclops Polyphemus, Odysseus says his name is Outis, \"Nobody.\" When the blinded giant shouts \"Nobody is hurting me,\" the other Cyclopes do not come."}},{"id":"menon_name","cat":"words","ch":"menon","name":{"en":"Menon"},"story":{"en":"On the evening the line broke, he held the ditch before the Ios ships with ninety-three men; sixty-one lived. The next morning, men from other contingents pointed at him and said: menōn. The one who stayed."},"hist":{"en":"Ancient Greek μένων, from the verb \"to stay, to wait.\" Menon was also a real Greek name; one of Plato's dialogues is called Meno. The Trojans' mēnis (wrath) sounds much like it."}}]},"chapters":{"net":{"pages":[{"en":"The royal city of Ios stood on the hilltop. It was a hill that had learned to command."},{"en":"Below it, in the fishing village by the sea, Seyagales was mending a net."},{"en":"He used a bone needle. He could not read, but he could count: one knot, two knots. The holes grew smaller one by one."},{"en":"He liked the sea. The sea did not ask him to become anything."},{"en":"His mother's hands smelled of fish and ash. She called him in to eat. Just a moment, he said. Three more knots."},{"en":"All he wanted was for tomorrow to be like today."}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"Three more knots."},"options":[{"label":{"en":"Finish them first"},"reply":{"en":"You finished. The net was good. So was the fish soup that night."}},{"label":{"en":"Go eat first"},"reply":{"en":"You would finish tomorrow. Tomorrow always comes, you thought."}}]}},"name":{"pages":[{"en":"The day the men from the royal city came to the village, the sea was calm."},{"en":"The one in front wore a linen robe and a seal around his neck. They wanted a boy."},{"en":"His mother stepped in front of him, as if her body could be a wall."},{"en":"In the end, it was she who said his name."},{"en":"Someone asked about his father. \"I don't have one,\" he said."},{"en":"A boy carrying a bundle of spears bigger than himself looked back at him, as if he were sorry, though he had done nothing."},{"en":"His mother stood outside the gate and did not move. She looked smaller."}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"At the gate."},"options":[{"label":{"en":"Ask the guard his name"},"reply":{"en":"The soldier looked at you, then told you. It was the first name you learned in the royal city."}},{"label":{"en":"Look back at your mother"},"reply":{"en":"She was still standing there. You walked on, and she was still standing there."}}]}},"stables":{"pages":[{"en":"The lower yard of the royal city smelled of horses."},{"en":"He carried a wooden tablet sealed with black wax. The keeper was broad-shouldered, his leather apron stained, and he said little."},{"en":"The keeper glanced at the tablet. \"Forget the tablet. You will sleep here tonight.\""},{"en":"The place to sleep was a long room under the storehouse."},{"en":"Lykos was missing a front tooth, asked questions without stopping, and kept finding ways out of sweeping. Pheres had a scar on his chin and paid no one much attention."},{"en":"That night he thought of the net. Three knots left."}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"Lykos asks where you're from."},"options":[{"label":{"en":"\"By the sea.\""},"reply":{"en":"Lykos asked three more questions. You answered them one by one until someone told you both to be quiet."}},{"label":{"en":"Don't answer"},"reply":{"en":"Pheres glanced at you, turned over, and went to sleep."}}]}},"scar":{"pages":[{"en":"The man was older than the keeper and broader than most of the soldiers. Grey at the temples."},{"en":"A pale scar ran from his left ear to the corner of his mouth, so that side of his mouth always seemed to lift a little."},{"en":"His name was Mnes. He did not shout, unless someone had already made a serious mistake."},{"en":"When it was time to move, Seyagales was still asking questions. Mnes struck him."},{"en":"\"Questions are useful,\" Mnes said. \"So is silence.\""},{"en":"Later he said, \"Do not mistake anger for a road.\""},{"en":"Mnes kept him close, as a messenger boy."}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"Your cheek still stings."},"options":[{"label":{"en":"Glare at him"},"reply":{"en":"Mnes looked back at you until you looked away first."}},{"label":{"en":"Shut up and move"},"reply":{"en":"You moved. Mnes said nothing at all."}}]}},"east":{"pages":[{"en":"They gave him a bronze helmet too big for him, packed with leather. The sandals did not fit and soon split."},{"en":"His old clothes stayed by the bed in the room under the storehouse."},{"en":"In another, deeper harbor lay ships painted with pitch. Braziers burned, and a priest poured wine on the altar."},{"en":"The horn sounded. The ships went east."},{"en":"The sea was the same sea. In his head he counted the three knots still missing from the net."}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"The ship pulls away from shore."},"options":[{"label":{"en":"Watch Ios"},"reply":{"en":"The city on the hill grew smaller. The village below it could no longer be seen."}},{"label":{"en":"Look ahead"},"reply":{"en":"To the east there was only sea. You did not yet know what that place was called."}}]}},"knot":{"pages":[{"en":"The ship made Seyagales ill before midnight. He had thought the sea would be different once it carried him away from Ios. It was not."},{"en":"Lykos lay beside a coil of rope, his face the color of old ash. \"If you are going to die,\" he said, \"do it over the side.\""},{"en":"A sailor pushed a wooden bowl into his hands. \"Use this.\" \"For what?\" The sailor kept walking. Seyagales decided that questions were not always useful."},{"en":"Mnes checked the leather strap still tied around his wrist. \"You kept it.\" \"It was given to me.\" \"Many things are given to men so they can be taken away later.\""},{"en":"He dreamed of the shore. His mother was repairing a net. She had no needle; she used a small bronze sword. Each time she pulled the blade through the mesh, the sea rose higher around her feet."},{"en":"By midday more ships appeared to the east, their sails the color of bone. \"Then why are they going?\" Mnes looked at the ships. \"Because kings rarely need only their own men.\""},{"en":"That evening the sailors made him help secure the water jars. He tied the first knot badly, and water ran across the deck. The sailor tied it again. \"Watch.\" He untied it. \"Now.\" One tug. It held. \"Again.\""},{"en":"At sunset Mnes came to stand beside him. \"You will remember that knot?\" \"Yes.\" \"What is it called?\" \"A knot.\""}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"Mnes looks back at you. For a moment his scar makes his face seem amused."},"options":[{"label":{"en":"Tug the knot once more"},"reply":{"en":"It looked weaker than the knots you used on nets. It held. The ship went on east through the dark."}},{"label":{"en":"Look back"},"reply":{"en":"Ios was behind you. The sea no longer had a shore you could recognize."}}]}},"line":{"pages":[{"en":"They reached land on the third morning. The coast was flat and yellow. There were no walls and no city. The army had made its own city beside the water."},{"en":"The camp had no single smell: horses, onions, sweat, wet leather, smoke, sickness, and the sea. Lykos nearly fell into a pile of reeds. \"It is still moving.\" \"The land?\" \"Everything.\""},{"en":"The camp official marked his tablet. \"Your people go to the eastern line.\" \"We have no line,\" Mnes said. \"You do now. Find the black standard. If you find the white one, you have gone too far.\""},{"en":"Mnes put him with the message runners. \"You will carry words.\" \"What if someone gives me something?\" \"Ask whether it is yours to carry.\" \"What if he says yes?\" \"Then use your judgment.\" Judgment had become another name for being struck."},{"en":"The captain was asleep beneath a cart; his servant reached for the tablet. \"Your name?\" \"Philon.\" \"Are you the captain?\" \"No.\" The servant snatched it. The captain woke, read it, and struck the servant with the back of his hand. \"Do not take messages from children.\""},{"en":"The eastern line was not a wall. It was a row of stakes driven into the ground, with ropes stretched between them. A man stood there watching the hills. \"How many ships?\" \"I don't know.\" \"How many men?\" \"I don't know.\" \"Then what use are you?\""},{"en":"Seyagales thought about the question. \"I brought the tablet.\" The man looked at him for a long moment, then turned back toward the hills. \"That is one use.\" The hills were empty. Seyagales did not believe them."},{"en":"That night the men near the fires stopped laughing. Mnes scraped mud from his sandals. \"Are we going to fight?\" \"Probably.\" \"When?\" \"Soon.\" \"Against whom?\" Mnes looked toward the dark hills. \"A city.\""}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"\"A city.\""},"options":[{"label":{"en":"Wait for more"},"reply":{"en":"You waited for more. Mnes gave you none."}},{"label":{"en":"Look up at the stars"},"reply":{"en":"Above the camp the stars were sharp and numerous. You wondered how many men had looked at them from this shore before you. You wondered whether the stars remembered."}}]}},"horse":{"pages":[{"en":"The army did not move the next day. It moved around itself. A group of soldiers was sent toward the hills and returned before noon. Nothing came back with them except dust."},{"en":"At the horse lines, one of the animals began to scream. It was a tall gray horse with a white mark down its face. A boy was trying to pull its head toward the trough. The animal reared. The boy fell beneath it."},{"en":"Seyagales moved before he understood that he had moved. He seized the bridle. The horse pulled; he struck the ground, and the bridle burned through his palm."},{"en":"The soldiers pulled the boy free. His tunic had torn open at the side. There was not much blood. There was enough."},{"en":"\"You should not have touched the horse,\" Mnes said as he wrapped the cut. \"The boy was beneath it.\" \"I saw.\" \"Then why say it?\" \"Because seeing a thing does not make it wise.\""},{"en":"\"Will it be killed?\" \"Probably not.\" \"Why?\" \"Because it is valuable.\" The answer stayed with Seyagales longer than the pain in his hand."},{"en":"By evening the boy had not returned. No one said whether he was alive. The camp continued to move around the absence of him. Someone ate beside the place where he had slept. Someone else borrowed his knife."},{"en":"\"Are you afraid?\" \"Of what?\" \"The city. The war.\" Mnes turned back toward the hills. \"You are afraid of the wrong thing.\" \"What should I be afraid of?\" \"Everything. Then choose.\""},{"en":"The horns sounded from the center of the camp. Fires were covered. Horses were saddled. \"We are moving at first light.\" \"Toward the city?\" Mnes looked east. \"Toward Troy.\""}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"The name meant nothing to him. It entered the night anyway."},"options":[{"label":{"en":"Repeat it once"},"reply":{"en":"You repeated it once in your mind, carefully, as if it were a knot you had been told not to lose."}},{"label":{"en":"Look at your hand"},"reply":{"en":"Under the linen the straight red line was still there. It was your blood. It was still blood."}}]}},"count":{"pages":[{"en":"The army left the shore at first light and walked inland toward a city no one had seen. Lykos talked the whole way about the bulls his uncle had seen on Crete. At last he said, \"You are very tiring,\" and went to walk beside Pheres instead."},{"en":"The men of Ios were given a flat, stinking piece of ground. \"No one else wants it,\" said Mnes, \"so no one will take it from us.\" \"It stinks.\" \"So will you, soon.\""},{"en":"Then they saw Troy. The hill on Ios had learned to command. These walls had learned something worse. They had learned to wait."},{"en":"A herald walked the line while a scribe read from a tablet: \"Ios. Of the house of King Agallos. Twelve ships. Six hundred men.\""},{"en":"Bored in the line, Seyagales counted. The men standing. The men cooking. The men on the ships. Mnes. Peisandros and his men. And himself."},{"en":"\"There are not six hundred,\" he said. \"There are four hundred and eighty-seven.\" \"Who told you that?\" \"No one. I counted.\" \"Count them again.\" \"I did. Three times with the ships.\""},{"en":"Mnes looked at him for a long time. \"Who else have you told?\" \"No one.\" \"Then don't.\""},{"en":"That night, lying on the stinking ground, he counted the number once more in his head. Four hundred and eighty-seven. Like a knot he must not lose."}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"The herald has walked on. The number on the tablet is still six hundred."},"options":[{"label":{"en":"Count again"},"reply":{"en":"Four hundred and eighty-seven. Every time, four hundred and eighty-seven."}},{"label":{"en":"Look at the walls"},"reply":{"en":"The walls did nothing. They only waited."}}]}},"truce":{"pages":[{"en":"The war did not begin the way he had imagined. He did not see the fighting. He saw what came after it."},{"en":"In the first month, Lykos went to the river with a water party and did not come back. \"We should go and look.\" \"It is dark,\" said Mnes, \"and the men who were there are still there.\""},{"en":"There was a truce to gather the dead. Mnes gave him a jar. \"You will carry water.\" \"Why water?\" \"You will see.\""},{"en":"\"Wash their faces,\" said Mnes. \"So the men can see who they are.\""},{"en":"He found Lykos under the willows. He washed the face, all the way to the missing front tooth."},{"en":"Across the river, a tall Trojan was washing his own dead with his own hands. He saw the boy. \"Your brother?\" \"No. Lykos.\" \"And you?\" \"Seyagales.\""},{"en":"\"That is a name for a fisherman.\" \"I am a fisherman.\" The man looked at him. \"Not here.\""},{"en":"That night at the fire, Mnes told him who the man was. Hector, the son of the king of Troy. From that day, Seyagales began to keep names. He never decided to."}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"The Trojan said: \"Not here.\""},"options":[{"label":{"en":"\"I am still a fisherman.\""},"reply":{"en":"He did not answer. He bent his head and went on washing his dead."}},{"label":{"en":"Nod"},"reply":{"en":"He nodded back. The river went on between you."}}]}},"winter":{"pages":[{"en":"The camp became a town. It grew its own roads, its own market, its own sickness. Even the stinking ditch became a wall."},{"en":"When the grain ships were late, everyone went hungry. He learned that the Ios stores were always shorter than the tablets said. \"Never more?\" \"Once. One extra jar of wine.\" \"Where did it go?\" \"To Peisandros's tent.\""},{"en":"Peisandros was Cleon's nephew, and he commanded the men of Ios. He ate well."},{"en":"An older Ios boy, Glaukos, stole his ration. Seyagales broke his nose with a water jar."},{"en":"Mnes said nothing for a whole day. Then: \"Next time, do it where everyone can see. So that it only has to be done once.\" He paused. \"Or don't do it.\""},{"en":"\"I wanted to hit him again.\" \"Yes,\" said Mnes. \"That happens.\" \"Does it stop?\" \"No. But you get better at hearing it coming.\""},{"en":"The split sandal finally gave way. A shard of bronze in the sand cut into his heel and left a small scar shaped like a new moon."}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"Glaukos sits on the sand, holding his nose. Everyone is watching."},"options":[{"label":{"en":"Offer him a hand"},"reply":{"en":"He did not take your hand. But he never touched your ration again."}},{"label":{"en":"Walk away"},"reply":{"en":"Someone laughed behind you. You did not know who they were laughing at."}}]}},"tablet":{"pages":[{"en":"The third year. Peisandros decided to take the men of Ios against the Scaean gate. \"The kings have not ordered it.\" \"The kings will thank us.\""},{"en":"He did not come back. Forty-one of the men who went with him did not come back either."},{"en":"The nobles of Ios began to quarrel over who would command. Alkmes's family said it should be theirs."},{"en":"Mnes brought out a tablet sealed with black wax. He had carried it for more than two years. \"I was told to open it if the commander fell. The commander has fallen.\""},{"en":"The scribe read it aloud: \"Agallos, King of Ios, to the men of Ios at Troy. The boy Seyagales, who was taken from the House of Thestor below the city, is my son.\""},{"en":"The boy who had said \"I don't have one\" heard his father's name from a stranger's mouth. Men laughed. Then they stopped."},{"en":"\"You expect me to take orders from a fourteen-year-old fisherman?\" said Alkmes. \"No,\" said Mnes. \"The king does.\""},{"en":"That night he asked Mnes, \"Did you know?\" \"Yes.\" \"Since when?\" \"Since before you did.\""}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"Everyone is looking at you. Pheres looks at you differently now."},"options":[{"label":{"en":"Look at Mnes"},"reply":{"en":"Mnes called you \"lord.\" It was the first time."}},{"label":{"en":"Look at the sea"},"reply":{"en":"The sea was the same sea. It did not know who the king was."}}]}},"alkmes":{"pages":[{"en":"The grain ships were late again. Sosias reckoned it: at the present rations, twelve days."},{"en":"Seyagales knew there were eleven jars of barley under Alkmes's bed. \"I wasn't looking for them. They were there.\" All the nobles' grain together would last thirty-one days."},{"en":"He gave the order: the nobles' grain would be shared with the shore men."},{"en":"Alkmes refused in front of everyone. \"My grain is my family's grain. I don't choose to share it with fish.\" \"It's an order.\" \"It's a child talking. Go and carry something.\""},{"en":"\"If this passes,\" said Mnes, \"I cannot hold them. It is your voice now, not mine.\""},{"en":"He tried everything else first. Alkmes laughed at the bastard."},{"en":"He gave the order. Amphios carried it out: the boy with the spears who had looked back, the day they came to the shore. Seyagales made himself watch."},{"en":"Afterward, for the first time, he was sick. Then he asked for Alkmes's father's name, his house, his brothers. He added them to the names."},{"en":"In the morning, all the grain was in the storehouse. No one ever refused him again, not in front of the others. He did not know whether this meant he had done the right thing. He suspected it did not mean that at all."}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"In the dark, Mnes asks: \"How many is that?\""},"options":[{"label":{"en":"\"Ninety-six.\""},"reply":{"en":"\"You know all of them.\" Mnes looked at you in the dark for a long time. \"Gods help you.\" It was not clear to whom he was saying it."}},{"label":{"en":"Say nothing"},"reply":{"en":"You said the names again in your head, from the first. The last one was Alkmes."}}]}},"eurion":{"pages":[{"en":"Eurion came from Ios with forty reinforcements. On the voyage he had heard: the king's bastard was a child who had executed a noble."},{"en":"He expected a monster. Or a puppet."},{"en":"He found a fifteen-year-old boy counting jars. \"From Ios? How many?\" \"Forty.\" \"Thirty-nine.\" Eurion looked around. Glaukon's idiot brother was missing."},{"en":"\"What's your name?\" \"Eurion.\" \"From where?\" \"The western hills. Above the bay of the black rocks.\" \"Have you been in a war?\" \"Pirates.\" \"Did you like it?\" \"No.\" \"Good. Go to sleep, Eurion.\""},{"en":"The next morning, the boy remembered his name. And everyone else's. \"Glaukon's idiot brother.\" \"It's Doryklos!\" \"I know. I wanted to see if you knew.\""},{"en":"The boy's first plan: hide in the reed marsh at night and ambush the Trojan foragers. \"This?\" said Eurion. \"You want me to do this?\""},{"en":"It worked. Eurion was irritated that it worked."}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"The boy asks Eurion: \"Did you like it? The war?\""},"options":[{"label":{"en":"\"No.\""},"reply":{"en":"\"Good,\" he said. As if it were the rightest thing you had ever said."}},{"label":{"en":"\"Who would?\""},"reply":{"en":"\"Plenty of people,\" he said. \"Go to sleep, Eurion.\""}}]}},"water":{"pages":[{"en":"He watched where the women went for water at dawn. An old stonecutter, a prisoner, told him: there was a spring cave in the rock under the wall."},{"en":"\"If water can go in,\" said Seyagales, \"so can a man.\""},{"en":"Odysseus sat down in front of the Ios hut as if it belonged to him. \"So. You're the one who watches women go to the well.\" \"Yes.\" \"Good. Most men watch them come back.\""},{"en":"\"And the men who go in, how do they come out?\" \"The way they went in.\" \"With the city awake and on fire?\" \"Yes.\" \"How many come back?\" \"I don't know.\" Odysseus stood up. \"That is the first honest thing a commander has said to me in four years.\""},{"en":"Twelve men crawled into the water channel at night. Seyagales, Eurion, Pheres, Amphios, and eight others."},{"en":"In the stone house at the top, a Trojan boy of about twelve was carrying a water jar too large for him. He saw them."},{"en":"They fired the granary. Four died getting out."},{"en":"The next day Odysseus asked, \"Who thought of the water?\" Seyagales thought of the jar on the boy's hip."}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"The boy has seen you. He holds the jar and makes no sound."},"options":[{"label":{"en":"Nod"},"reply":{"en":"You nodded. Eurion moved. For many years afterward, you would remember that nod."}},{"label":{"en":"Close your eyes"},"reply":{"en":"When you opened your eyes, the boy was gone. Eurion would not look at you."}}]}},"menis":{"pages":[{"en":"The fifth year to the ninth. The days broke into pieces."},{"en":"The Trojans had a name for the men of Ios: mēnis. Wrath. The anger of the gods, the kind that doesn't stop. The army took it up: the Wrath of Ios. He hated it."},{"en":"At a fire, Odysseus said he had once told a man his name was Nobody. \"It's the best name I ever had. No one can hold it against you.\""},{"en":"Mnes's knees went. He began to walk leaning on his spear."},{"en":"In the seventh year, a tablet came from Ios. The scribe read it to him the way he read grain counts. His mother was dead."},{"en":"\"Thank you,\" he said. It was the only thing he could find to say. He took the tablet he could not read and walked away down the beach."},{"en":"In seven years he had said the names of a hundred and ninety dead men. He had never said hers. She was the one person in the world he didn't have to count."},{"en":"That night he went down to the sea. He did not go in."}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"The scribe says: \"I'm sorry.\""},"options":[{"label":{"en":"\"Thank you.\""},"reply":{"en":"You said thank you again. Because it was the only thing you could find."}},{"label":{"en":"Take the tablet back"},"reply":{"en":"You could not read it. You carried it all the way to the sea anyway."}}]}},"oldman":{"pages":[{"en":"The tenth year. Hector was dead. Seyagales watched the body dragged past the ships."},{"en":"That night he stood sentry at the edge of Achilles's camp."},{"en":"An old man in a cloak drove a mule cart out of the dark. A young man walked beside it, and left no footprints in the wet sand."},{"en":"He should have challenged them. He looked at the old man's face. He let them pass."},{"en":"Later, from the dark, he saw the old man kneel and kiss the hands of the man who had killed his son."},{"en":"\"Why did you let him through?\" Mnes asked. \"I don't know. He looked at me. And I thought of… my father.\" \"Your father is not that kind of man.\" \"I know.\" \"But you'd want him to be.\""},{"en":"On the walls of Troy, lamps were burning everywhere, in no order at all. The city was mourning its son."},{"en":"\"I didn't know you could do that,\" Seyagales said. \"Let someone go. Not because you can't stop them. Because you choose not to.\" Mnes drank. \"Most men never find out.\""}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"The old man stops in front of you. He says nothing."},"options":[{"label":{"en":"Let him pass"},"reply":{"en":"You stepped aside. As he passed you, he nodded once."}},{"label":{"en":"Ask his name"},"reply":{"en":"He told you. You had already known. You stepped aside anyway."}}]}},"menon":{"pages":[{"en":"Achilles was dead. The army was shaken."},{"en":"At dusk the Trojans reached the ships. The line broke. The order to fall back ran down the beach."},{"en":"He did not fall back. If the ships burned, no one went home. He held the ditch before the Ios ships with ninety-three men. Mnes stayed, because the boy stayed."},{"en":"They held until dark and the relief. Of the ninety-three, sixty-one lived."},{"en":"In the morning, men from other contingents pointed at him and said a word: menōn. The one who stayed."},{"en":"\"They're calling you something,\" said Eurion. \"Better than wrath.\" \"I know my name.\""},{"en":"He thought: there is no one left alive who calls me by my name except Mnes. And then he thought: and Mnes calls me lord."},{"en":"In the evening he walked into the sea and washed the ditch off himself. On the beach, men stopped to watch. They did not see a boy. They had not seen a boy for some time."},{"en":"When he was clean, Menon came out of the water, put on his tunic, and went back up the beach to count the barley."}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"Eurion says: \"They're calling you Menon.\""},"options":[{"label":{"en":"\"I know my name.\""},"reply":{"en":"\"I know you do,\" said Eurion. \"I'm just telling you what they're calling you.\""}},{"label":{"en":"Say nothing"},"reply":{"en":"Outside, the new name went up and down the beach like the sea."}}]}},"wooden_horse":{"pages":[{"en":"The wooden horse. The Ios ships burned their camp, pretended to leave, and came back in the dark."},{"en":"The city fell. He kept his own men from the worst of it. He could not keep anyone else."},{"en":"He saw a Trojan woman washing the feet of a dead child."},{"en":"He took nothing from Troy."},{"en":"On the beach, he counted. Not with his eyes; in his head, starting with Lykos. Of four hundred and eighty-seven men taken from Ios ten years ago, one hundred and nine were going home."},{"en":"That night he lay on the sand and said the other three hundred and seventy-eight names. Each man's father, his house, how he died. It took until dawn."},{"en":"Somewhere in the middle, he became aware that Mnes was awake, listening. Beyond Mnes, Eurion. Then Pheres. Amphios. Others. No one interrupted. No one went to sleep."},{"en":"When he reached the last name, a voice in the dark quietly said one more. The boy with the water jar. Not his real name, which no one would ever know, but the name the Wrath had given him."},{"en":"Menon said it too, quietly, at the end of the list, where it belonged. Three hundred and seventy-nine."}],"choice":{"prompt":{"en":"Dawn is coming. The ridge where Troy once stood is turning gray."},"options":[{"label":{"en":"Count again"},"reply":{"en":"One hundred and nine. Still one hundred and nine."}},{"label":{"en":"Listen to the sea"},"reply":{"en":"The waves struck the shore, withdrew into the dark, and returned. They did not know what you had counted."}}]}}}}};window.MENON_LATE_LANG="en";